{"chunk_id": "fcb78d8206c3", "text": "Victor works alone in his island laboratory finishing the female companion he promised the Creature. As the moon rises, he imagines the consequences: the new being might reject the Creature, become even more violent, or reproduce a race of monsters that could threaten humanity. Horrified by the moral weight of his promise, Victor suddenly sees the Creature watching through the window. In a surge of resolve he tears the unfinished body apart. The Creature responds with despair and fury, vowing revenge and delivering the ominous threat: he will be with Victor on his wedding night. Victor disposes of the remains at sea but is blown off course in a storm and lands in an unfamiliar town, where hostile locals accuse him of involvement in a recent murder\u2014setting up the next catastrophe.\nVictor destroys the unfinished female creature; the monster vows revenge on his wedding night, and Victor later drifts to Ireland where he is accused of murder.\nThemes: moral responsibility, revenge, creator vs creation, isolation, fear of consequences", "vector": [0.0001178520469693467, -0.030522199347615242, 0.0041876621544361115, 0.002616865560412407, -0.015911083668470383, 0.01335176918655634, -0.019486000761389732, -0.00659802183508873, 0.005595962051302195, -0.019783910363912582, 0.005656898021697998, 0.045823920518159866, 0.005585805978626013, -0.021869277581572533, 0.011814826168119907, 0.010684123262763023, 0.04308857023715973, -0.00588710093870759, 0.020488059148192406, -0.028436830267310143, -0.0012390334159135818, 0.015125686302781105, 0.010697664692997932, -0.00219877646304667, -0.014394452795386314, -0.006506617646664381, 0.014665280468761921, -0.028409749269485474, 0.0190662182867527, -0.010988804511725903, -0.0026388701517134905, -0.007975853979587555, -0.011835138313472271, -0.017075639218091965, -0.03320338577032089, 0.010636729188263416, 0.007041500881314278, -0.015518384985625744, 0.008815417997539043, -0.011354420334100723, 0